  For stmap46 this predicate is used to bypass the pressure-agreement fallback, but it only checks arrival gain. Any candidate already in the middle-relief window can therefore take the one-inverter exception with slack as loose as `2 * SlackMargin`, which is broader than the advertised tight-critical exception and can admit pressure-disagreed cuts that this mode is meant to keep blocked.
The stmap46 exception is wider than the intended tight-critical path and can change mapper decisions for loose high-gain candidates without pressure agreement.

